open-grind (0.1.0-rc.1) beta; urgency=medium

  First release candidate for v0.1.0.

  - Location messages added to chats
  - Profile photo replies added
  - Album replies and reactions added
  - GIFs and Gaymoji added to chats
  - Paste, drag and drop photos and videos into chats, albums and profile
    photos, including images dragged out of a browser
  - "I'm Into" and "Vaccinated for" added to profiles
  - "Tribes They're Into" grid filter added
  - Notifications are now supported

  Full changelog:
  https://s.opengrind.org/changelogs/v0.1.0-rc.1

 -- Open Grind Governance <https://opengrind.org/governance>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0100

open-grind (0.1.0-beta.5.1) beta; urgency=medium

  Follow-up update to v0.1.0-beta.5 with bug fixes and cosmetic improvements.

  - Fixed the Honduras bypass
  - Block button is available again, ignoring server's "non-blockable
    profile" flag
  - Fixed unresponsive profiles opened deep in the Browse grid
  - Fixed Men/Cis Man/Trans Man and Women/Cis Woman/Trans Woman chips in
    filters
  - The grid now scrolls to top when changing filters or location and
    tapping "Retry"
  - Fixed the nav bar avatar not updating after a photo change
  - Fixed Refresh button reveal animation FPS on Linux
  - Fixed Hidden users list not showing recently hidden in current session
    users
  - Fixed photo carousel photos bleeding alignment
  - Visual improvements to dropdowns positioning, dividers at edges, gender
    chips reveal animation
  - Fixed pull-to-refresh at the newest message on scaled displays
  - Fixed Refresh button appearing in short conversation when wheeling up
  - Fixed deep scroll restoration on the Inbox page after switching tabs
  - Fixed number of columns in the Albums tab in the media attachments
    drawer
  - Fixed inconsistent media tile menu positioning
  - Improved media drag'n'drop positioning
  - Fixed failing Browse page retrying in a loop
  - Fixed infinite scroll stalling when its trigger leaves and re-enters
    view in one batch
  - Fixed overlapping preferences saves corrupting them
  - Fixed detached earlier rows in sliding-out Credits page
  - Improved spinners/skeletons usage consistency in app design
  - API UA moved from 26.18.0 to 26.20.0
  - Community translations portal opens in the coming days

  Full changelog:
  https://git.opengrind.org/open-grind/open-grind/compare/v0.1.0-beta.5...v0.1.0-beta.5.1

 -- Open Grind Governance <https://opengrind.org/governance>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 21:31:56 +0200
